# Hermes Admin App

Welcome to the Hermes Admin App - A comprehensive administrative dashboard for managing your application efficiently.

## 📋 Table of Contents
- [Overview](#overview)
- [Features](#features)
- [Installation](#installation)
- [Usage](#usage)
- [Documentation](#documentation)

## Overview

Hermes Admin App is a modern, user-friendly administrative interface designed to streamline your management workflows. Built with responsive design principles, it provides a seamless experience across all devices.

## ✨ Features

- **Dashboard**: Real-time analytics and metrics overview
- **User Management**: Create, update, and manage user accounts
- **Reporting**: Generate comprehensive reports and exports
- **Settings**: Configurable application preferences
- **Notifications**: Real-time alerts and notifications system
- **Security**: Role-based access control (RBAC)

## 🚀 Installation

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/HermesAdminApp.git

# Navigate to project directory
cd HermesAdminApp

# Install dependencies
npm install

# Start the application
npm start
```

## 📖 Documentation

### Notes
> **Important**: Always ensure you have proper authentication credentials before accessing the admin panel.
> 
> The application uses JWT tokens for session management. Keep your tokens secure and never share them publicly.

### Getting Started
1. Log in with your admin credentials
2. Navigate to the Dashboard to view system metrics
3. Access User Management to administer accounts
4. Configure settings as needed in the Settings panel

### Key Components
- **Authentication Module**: Handles user login and session management
- **Database Layer**: Manages all data persistence
- **API Gateway**: Provides RESTful endpoints for frontend communication
- **Admin Interface**: User-friendly dashboard for all operations

### API Endpoints
- `GET /api/users` - Retrieve all users
- `POST /api/users` - Create new user
- `PUT /api/users/:id` - Update user information
- `DELETE /api/users/:id` - Remove user account
- `GET /api/reports` - Generate reports

## 🔧 Configuration

Edit the `.env` file to configure:
```
DATABASE_URL=your_database_url
API_PORT=3000
JWT_SECRET=your_secret_key
```

## 📝 Additional Notes

- Ensure Node.js v14+ is installed
- Database migrations run automatically on startup
- For production deployment, set NODE_ENV=production
- Regular backups are recommended for data safety

## 🤝 Support

For issues or questions, please create an issue in the repository or contact the development team.

